# Redesign project cards

Use `GroveCard` + `.grove*` styles as the reference when building or updating project cards.

## Project-specific data

Update title, tagline, brandColor, href, and cardImage **only** in [`app/redesign/projects.ts`](app/redesign/projects.ts). Do not hardcode those fields in card components.

Pass brand via CSS var `--card-brand` on the card root. Layout positions stay in `redesign.module.css` (map `id → styles.*` in the board).

## Shared typography (must match across cards)

| Role | Size | Weight | Line-height | Opacity |
|------|------|--------|-------------|---------|
| Title | `clamp(0.875rem, 1.3vw, 1.375rem)` | 700 | 1.2 | 100% |
| Tagline | `clamp(0.75rem, 1.05vw, 1.125rem)` | 500 | 1.25 | 60% |

Mobile (≤900px) bumps titles to `clamp(1.125rem, 4.8vw, 1.5rem)` and taglines to `clamp(0.75rem, 3vw, 0.9375rem)`.

- Tagline is always smaller than title; use `text-transform: capitalize`.
- Across the redesign: headers/titles at `opacity: 1`, description/tagline copy at `opacity: 0.6` idle — full opacity on card hover / focus-visible / `data-card-active`.
- Text block: absolute inset from design px ÷ card size; column with `justify-content: space-between`.
- Hover / play colors: wire both `:hover`/`:focus-visible` and `[data-card-active="true"]` so mobile tap-to-play matches desktop hover.

## Hover interaction

- Idle background: `#F2F2F2`
- Hover / focus-visible background: `var(--card-brand-hover, var(--card-brand))` (solid or gradient via optional `brandHover` in `projects.ts`)
- Idle text: `var(--card-brand)`; hover / focus-visible text: `#fff`
- Transition background/color ~`320ms ease` (use opacity crossfade when hover bg is a gradient)
- Honor `useReducedMotion()`: skip layer motion
- **Desktop:** start layer motion on card hover/focus only (`onPointerEnter` / `Leave`, `onFocus` / `Blur`)
- **Mobile (≤900px):** light mode keeps the full final hover pose at idle (brand bg + end-pose layers). Dark mode uses desktop idle (glass bg + rest pose). Use `useProjectCardNav(href)` so a tap runs the same rewind → play sequence (`data-card-replaying` then `data-card-active`), then navigates — dark goes from glass to brand on press. Reduced motion skips the play and navigates immediately.
- Non-project cards may still use `useCardHover()` (end pose on mobile) when they are not case-study links.

## Layer geometry (porting from Figma)

- **Prefer Figma "copy as code" absolute geometry** over deriving placement from nested wrappers/masks: one box in card coordinates (`left/top/width/height` from the design px ÷ card size) is simpler and far less fragile.
- Rotated layers: keep Figma's `transform-origin` (usually `top left` in copy-as-code output) — re-deriving a center-origin equivalent invites drift.
- Never put CSS `rotate` on a framer-motion element: motion overwrites `transform`. Motion wrapper = unrotated box (translate only); rotation goes on an inner element.
- Ignore Figma mask rectangles when the card's own `overflow: hidden` + `border-radius` already does the clipping (copy-as-code renders masks as grey `#D9D9D9` placeholder rects — don't implement those).

## Sizing chip/badge contents (container queries)

- `container-type` must go on the **parent frame**, not the element being sized: cq units (`cqw`/`cqh`) resolve against the nearest *ancestor* container. An element can't be its own container — without an ancestor container, cq units silently fall back to viewport units and blow up padding/font (symptom: giant empty pill, text clipped by `overflow: hidden`).
- Compute cq values as design px ÷ container frame size, and note the math in a comment (e.g. `11.11cqw /* 20 ÷ 180 */`).
- `container-type: size` doesn't clip — children can still animate outside the frame.

## Motion

- One-shot only — never `repeat: Infinity`
- Shared hover spring across cards: `{ type: "spring", duration: 0.4, bounce: 0.28 }`; leave uses `{ type: "spring", duration: 0.28, bounce: 0 }`
- Animate to end pose values (not keyframe arrays); use `delay` for stagger between layers
- Prefer motion offsets as `%` of the layer’s own size when layout is `%`-based (fixed px breaks when the card scales)
- Rest = Figma t=0; hold end pose while hovered — rest position is the node's static frame position

## Image assets

- **Never remove backgrounds or post-process exported images** (no flood-fill, color-keying, or alpha edits). The Figma assets are already prepped for export with transparent backgrounds — use them as-is (downscaling for file size is OK).
- If a node export comes back with the card background baked in (opaque alpha), don't "fix" it in post — download the node's **raw source images** instead (`download_assets` → `rawImages`); those are the prepped transparent assets.
- Do not crop: `object-contain` on layered PNGs (not `object-cover`)
- Prefer `fill` + percentage bounds from Figma
- Transparent Figma exports: `unoptimized` + cache-bust `?v=` when re-exporting
- Rotated nested assets: overflow visible on the motion wrapper; rotate an inner element if the export is unrotated
